  "reason": "Evidence: config_009 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the best so far at 0.518 acc / 0.484 F1, outperforming config_001 (same but transformer aggregation) by ~1.1% acc and ~2.9% F1. The fusion strategy is the only untested variable within this otherwise-identical architecture. Question: Does weighted fusion (config_016) improve over simple concat while keeping the winning avgpool aggregation? This is a minimal, single-variable change from the current best, making it a clean exploitation step that will clarify whether fusion strategy is a meaningful lever. If weighted fusion helps, it opens a clear path to combine with other improvements; if not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can pivot to testing alternative encoders. Cost: expected ~7 GPU hours (same architecture as config_009, only fusion module changes), keeping total spend moderate with 7 experiments remaining."
}

